From 93402fd50df7dc43fe11d839564bdeb462eb0ba7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 03:27:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] cron: quota hold parks jobs on the routing pool's
 SubscriptionQuotaUnavailable refusal

Since 11-01 x-reply-discovery and bsky-reply-discovery re-fired hourly into a Codex window the
pool had already said was closed until 11-04 (resets_at), because cron/quota_hold only knew the
Codex 429 AuthError 'retry after Ns'. Root: each consumer kept its own list of quota exception
types, so the new pool refusal type silently bypassed the cron hold.

- agent.model_routing_unavailable.quota_wait_seconds: one typed mapping from every quota
  refusal (SubscriptionQuotaUnavailable / any 429 ModelRoutingError via resets_at, rate-limited
  AuthError via retry_after, ProviderFallbackError whose every route is one) to a wait.
- cron.quota_hold.hold_seconds_from_failure delegates to it; classify_failure_hold logs one
  'quota failure not held' WARNING when a quota-class failure maps to no hold (detection).
- tests: RuntimeError-from-refusal hold, passed/bogus reset, fallback chain, a real scheduler
  tick that parks next_run_at past the reset, and a contract test that enumerates every 429
  ModelRoutingError subclass in the tree and requires each to map to a hold.

Self-heal cron-0f5ca72d35.
